{
	"version": 5,
	"id": "B6BPJfMBvS6K-jeik",
	"notes": "A rank-and-file agent of an Inquisitor's retinue: ex-Guardsman, ex-Arbitrator, scholar, rogue trader scion, or reformed criminal — Inquisitorial acolytes are drawn from anywhere the Inquisition finds a useful skill set, per Eisenhorn's and Ravenor's ensemble casts. This is a generalist investigator/field-agent baseline; individual acolytes should reskin the skill list toward their actual background. Point math: ST 10 (+0), DX 12 (+40), IQ 13 (+60), HT 11 (+10) = 110; advantages +20; disadvantages -32; skills +100. Total 198 points, the low end of framework.md's \"Elite human (200-350)\" tier. No psychic abilities here — an acolyte with a sanctioned psyker gift should add traits from the separate psyker power library on top of this base.\n",
	"traits": [
		{
			"id": "t2MIVI8SooDm2gNC3",
			"name": "ST",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Acolytes are chosen for skills and usefulness, not physical extremes.\n\nDesign: ST 10 (baseline), 10 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 0
		},
		{
			"id": "tLiaJzk1362Sic8Gm",
			"name": "DX",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Competent but not elite combatants — most acolytes' real value is investigative, not martial.\n\nDesign: DX 12 (+2), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 40
		},
		{
			"id": "tdFGHUBaWtmJ7JZX_",
			"name": "IQ",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Inquisition recruits for intelligence and initiative above all; Eisenhorn's and Ravenor's retinues are consistently written as sharp, resourceful people.\n\nDesign: IQ 13 (+3), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 60
		},
		{
			"id": "tj9xjNJxZdqN77Xdp",
			"name": "HT",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Fieldwork for the Inquisition is hard on the body, if less uniformly brutal than front-line Guard service.\n\nDesign: HT 11 (+1), 10 pts/level (B14).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "tjUtqe5IZ93I3rMk8",
			"name": "Fit",
			"reference": "B55",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Kept in reasonable shape by an active, dangerous job.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Fit (B55), 5 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 5
		},
		{
			"id": "tcZPJH9A1mGF2L404",
			"name": "Combat Reflexes",
			"reference": "B43",
			"local_notes": "Lore: An acolyte who freezes under fire does not remain an acolyte for long.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Combat Reflexes (B43), 15 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 15
		},
		{
			"id": "tmQDutFGduBL5akL0",
			"name": "Duty (Inquisition)",
			"reference": "B133",
			"local_notes": "Lore: An acolyte or Interrogator serves at an Inquisitor's word, and an Inquisitor answers to their Ordo and (nominally) the wider Inquisition; refusal is itself grounds for suspicion of heresy.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Duty (B133), hazardous and frequent, as above.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Social",
				"Imperium",
				"Inquisition"
			],
			"base_points": -15
		},
		{
			"id": "tEo-FoodheTKfGhyo",
			"name": "Intolerance (Heretics)",
			"reference": "B140",
			"local_notes": "Lore: An acolyte's entire job is hunting heresy; most come to share their Inquisitor's zeal for it.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Intolerance (B140), narrow-category cost (-5).",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -5
		},
		{
			"id": "tOnolzUkh05hbJ3wT",
			"name": "Secret (Works for the Inquisition)",
			"reference": "B152",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Inquisitorial agents routinely operate under cover identities; being identified as Inquisition staff can get an agent killed by exactly the people they are investigating, or by a hostile Imperial official who resents being investigated at all.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Secret (B152), moderate exposure risk, -10.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Social",
				"Imperium",
				"Inquisition"
			],
			"base_points": -10
		},
		{
			"id": "tfbmf2_90JAdLwt5A",
			"name": "Nobody Trusts an Inquisitor's Agent",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Even loyal Imperial citizens tend to clam up around anyone connected to the Inquisition.\n\nDesign: Quirk (B9), roleplaying flag only.",
			"tags": [
				"Quirk",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -1
		},
		{
			"id": "tlDhDpuishEFUzY32",
			"name": "Suspicious of Everyone, Eventually",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The job trains acolytes out of taking anyone at face value for long.\n\nDesign: Quirk (B9), roleplaying flag only.",
			"tags": [
				"Quirk",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -1
		}
	],
	"skills": [
		{
			"id": "s5sC-R3aoM1JL3n5K",
			"name": "Guns",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A concealable sidearm (autopistol, laspistol, or stub revolver) is standard acolyte kit.\n\nDesign: DX+4 (16) for 12 points, Easy (B170).",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Inquisition"
